<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n378" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ac-clīno</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to lean on</i> or <i>against something</i> (not before the Aug. period; mostly <b>poet.</b>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">se acclinavit in illum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					5, 72</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">latus leoni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. Silv. 4, 2, 51</span></i>
			.—Most freq. in <i>part. pass.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">acclinatus: colla acclinata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 10, 268</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terrae acclinatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 14, 666</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">castra tumulo sunt acclinata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					44, 3, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">maria terris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. Silv. 5, 4, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, with se, <i>to incline
				to a thing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad causam senatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					4, 48, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
